From ceffe6acb571a5da303d3b3335cefbbea215e868 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 02:25:20 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] generic: standalone nft_flow_offload L2 bridge offload

Ship the nft_flow_offload bridge-offload series for pending-6.18 as
three consolidated patches (675-01 through 675-03). Uses the native
NFPROTO_BRIDGE chain path (nft_do_chain_bridge) directly, eliminating
the kmod-br-netfilter dependency. Bridged IP traffic traverses the
NFPROTO_BRIDGE NF_BR_FORWARD hook in __br_forward without any
netfilter involvement on the bridge family.

675-01: forward-path and bridge-VLAN infrastructure. Exports
__dev_fill_forward_path() accepting a caller-supplied
net_device_path_ctx, allowing callers to pre-populate context (e.g.
VLAN state) before the forward path walk; dev_fill_forward_path()
wraps it. Adds the br_vlan_get_offload_info_rcu() bridge helper
(skb VLAN tag id if present, PVID otherwise; single
br_port_get_rcu() lookup, RCU read lock held by caller).

675-02: bridge offload core. nft_flow_route() takes the L2 bridge path
for bridge-port ingress: minimal dst entries anchored to the bridge
master are allocated inline via rt_dst_alloc()/ip6_dst_alloc() and
shared across directions via dst_hold(), since nf_route() fails for
bridged-only prefixes; otherwise it falls back to L3 routing (with a
null-dst guard and dst cleanup on error paths).
nft_dev_fill_forward_path() takes the caller ctx and skips the neigh
lookup for already-resolved MACs. nft_dev_forward_path() copies MACs
from the packet header direction-aware and resolves VLAN context
(skb tag or PVID via the 675-01 helper; tag-only passthrough records
encap without ctx, both NF_FLOW_TABLE_ENCAP_MAX-guarded) into
ctx.vlan[] and info.encap[]. Also: indev tracked for all path types,
DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_UNTAG underflow guard, DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA handling,
NFPROTO_BRIDGE validation, and L3 protocol from the conntrack tuple.
Registers the NFPROTO_BRIDGE flowtable type by copying flowtable_inet
plus MODULE_ALIAS_NF_FLOWTABLE(AF_BRIDGE).

675-03: bridge conntrack VLAN/PPPoE support. Adds nf_ct_bridge_inner()
for a single outer VLAN tag or PPPoE encapsulation, extends
nf_bridge_frag_data, and handles defrag/refrag/frag_restore for the
encapsulated packets.

